  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital assistive technology accelerator programme and linking startup ecosystems in Norway and Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incubation program for Assistive Technology for disabled. The Project&#x2019;s planned effect(s) on society (Impact) is to create a more conducive enabling environment for entrepreneurs, start-ups, and SMEs in the field of Assistive Technology (AT), and better access to local and foreign investments in the AT sector. It will foster entrepreneurs by running programmes to help start-ups grow, and simultaneous work to build capacity and raise awareness within the ecosystem and among investors whilst deepening digital fluency among disabled innovators. Fundraising efforts will aim both at securing follow-on investment for accelerator graduates, as well as opportunities to co-fund accelerator activities. This will also include deepening cooperation with existing accelerators in the region. Through a rigorous reporting structure, the project will amplify the learnings to a wide audience. Specifically, it will connect: the Kenya and Norway innovation and entrepreneurship ecosystems, The intended target groups are high growth potential AT start-ups in Kenya and East Africa</narrative>
  </description>
